    "text": "To determine the number of carnations in the third bouquet, we start by using the information given about the average number of carnations in the bouquets. The average number of carnations in the three bouquets is 12. This means that the total number of carnations in all three bouquets combined is:\n\n\\[ 12 \\times 3 = 36 \\]\n\nWe know the number of carnations in the first and second bouquets. The first bouquet has 9 carnations, and the second bouquet has 14 carnations. Let \\( x \\) be the number of carnations in the third bouquet. The total number of carnations in all three bouquets can be expressed as:\n\n\\[ 9 + 14 + x = 36 \\]\n\nWe can simplify this equation by combining the known quantities:\n\n\\[ 23 + x = 36 \\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\), we subtract 23 from both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ x = 36 - 23 \\]\n\\[ x = 13 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of carnations in the third bouquet is \\(\\boxed{13}\\).",
